index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..04d9a8833386ffe4d8668731679c9f30cf1f0e4b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/styles/61-64-prompts.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+61-linocut.png
+Generate one fresh image from text only. Do not use any reference image or any previous image. Square 1024x1024. The character is a woman in her early 30s, shoulder-length curly auburn hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses, mustard-yellow knit sweater, enjoying coffee with a croissant nearby. The requested medium and style must fully determine anatomy, proportions, perspective, framing, color and lighting. No text, letters, captions, signatures, logos or watermarks. Use case: illustration-story. Authentic handmade TWO-COLOR LINOCUT PRINT, black ink and a single mustard ink layer on natural handmade paper. Bold hand-carved black contour lines, rough white gouge marks, dense expressive carved hatching, slight uneven ink coverage, visible paper fibers, strong simplified interlocking graphic shapes. A tight monumental left-facing PROFILE portrait in the left and upper part of the square: big stylized carved curls reaching her shoulders, round glasses in profile, a few strongly cut freckles. She lifts a small steaming cup to her lips with a delightfully angular carved hand. Her mustard sweater fills the lower left with gouge-cut knitting patterns. A boldly shaped croissant on the tilted tabletop occupies the lower right. Interpret auburn curls and tortoiseshell details within the strict black/mustard print palette. Radically graphic relief-print anatomy and flattened space, no realistic gradients, no photographic rendering or digital smoothness. The whole image itself is the printed artwork, no mockup.
+
+62-risograph.png
+Generate one fresh image from text only. Do not use any reference image or any previous image. Square 1024x1024. The character is a woman in her early 30s, shoulder-length curly auburn hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses, mustard-yellow knit sweater, enjoying coffee with a croissant nearby. The requested medium and style must fully determine anatomy, proportions, perspective, framing, color and lighting. No text, letters, captions, signatures, logos or watermarks. Use case: illustration-story. Authentic RISOGRAPH indie art zine print with fluorescent pink and electric blue ink, translucent purple overprints, coarse stochastic grain, slight visible color misregistration, patchy roller coverage, simple eccentric flat shapes on off-white paper. Composition is a playful extreme HIGH-ANGLE view of a cafe table, with a tiny foreshortened woman peeking from the upper right and an enormous coffee cup and saucer dominating the lower left. Her curly auburn hair becomes pink-and-blue looped shapes; face a flat freckled oval; oversize round tortoiseshell spectacles. A small mustard-yellow third spot ink shape marks her knitted sweater and its simple blue stitch dashes. Her very long cartoon arm reaches across the table to hold the cup, a graphic croissant floats on a flat plate near her. Unusual asymmetrical crop, diagonal table edge, open paper space, naive zine drawing, intentionally wobbly minimal linework. Pink and blue dominate everywhere with obvious ink overlaps; print-native shape abstraction, no photographic lighting, no rendered 3D volumes, no text whatsoever. The artwork fills the square, not a photograph of a zine.
+
+63-mid-century.png
+Generate one fresh image from text only. Do not use any reference image or any previous image. Square 1024x1024. The character is a woman in her early 30s, shoulder-length curly auburn hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses, mustard-yellow knit sweater, enjoying coffee with a croissant nearby. The requested medium and style must fully determine anatomy, proportions, perspective, framing, color and lighting. No text, letters, captions, signatures, logos or watermarks. Use case: illustration-story. 1950s Mary Blair / UPA mid-century modern illustration, an authentic whimsical textured gouache animation concept painting. WIDE FULL-BODY cafe scene with the small seated woman at a spindly round table, shown head to toe amid delightfully crooked geometric cafe architecture. Her legs are long tapered angular shapes, her torso a mustard-yellow trapezoid sweater with decorative knit marks, her tiny head has simplified freckles, oversized round tortoiseshell glasses and shoulder-length auburn curls made from rhythmic scalloped shapes. She joyfully lifts a tiny coffee cup while a stylized croissant rests on her table. Wildly childlike tilted perspective, impossibly angled chair, interlocking flat rectangles and triangles, whimsical stylized proportions. Bold unusual pairings of coral red, turquoise, plum, butter cream and mustard; dry-brush gouache texture, broad areas of rich matte paint, economical joyful facial marks. No central portrait composition; the miniature figure is integrated into a richly designed roomy square environment. No photographic realism, no 3D rendering, no realistic shading, no text/signage.
+
+64-latte-art.png
+Generate one fresh image from text only. Do not use any reference image or any previous image. Square 1024x1024. The character is a woman in her early 30s, shoulder-length curly auburn hair, freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses, mustard-yellow knit sweater, enjoying coffee with a croissant nearby. The requested medium and style must fully determine anatomy, proportions, perspective, framing, color and lighting. No text, letters, captions, signatures, logos or watermarks. Use case: photorealistic-natural. A real, exquisitely detailed TOP-DOWN food photograph of a ceramic latte cup and saucer on a cafe table, with a flaky golden croissant beside the cup. The ONLY depiction of the woman is an intricate latte-art portrait physically etched into the milk foam inside the cup. A shoulders-up portrait in white microfoam, espresso crema and subtly tinted edible milk foam: joyful freckled woman in her early 30s, shoulder-length auburn-colored curly hair made from fine looping crema lines, round tortoiseshell spectacles rendered in espresso, mustard-yellow knit sweater rendered in golden edible foam with tiny knit markings. Within this foam portrait her little hands hold a miniature coffee cup near her contented smile. Make it convincingly hand-etched latte foam art: slight fluid marbling, tiny bubbles, creamy meniscus, delicate coffee-brown pin-tool strokes merging with milk, rather than a photo printed on the surface. The circular latte surface fills much of the square, handle to one side, croissant on the table nearby, soft natural cafe window light, tactile ceramic, warm realistic wood and pastry flakes, straight overhead camera. No real woman outside the cup, no other portrait anywhere, no text, no watermark.
+

